    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: CHANGES REQUESTED\n\nThe refactor itself is clean and well-placed: the public-holiday rule lives in exactly the right unit (`BusinessDay`), the extraction of `isWeekend(...)` is a natural helper, and converting `rollForward` to a skip-loop over both weekends and holidays is the idiomatic way to express \"repeatedly advance to a clear business day.\" No duplication, no catch-all creep.\n\nOne concrete coherence finding:\n\n- **`effective(...)` javadoc is now stale** (`BusinessDay.java:47`). It still reads \"rolled forward off any weekend,\" but `effective` delegates to the same `rollForward` that now also skips public holidays. The diff updated the class-level and `rollForward` javadocs to mention holidays but left this one describing the old weekend-only behavior, so the three doc comments now disagree about what the method does. Update it to match (e.g. \"\u2026rolled forward off any weekend or public holiday\") so a maintainer reading `effective` in isolation isn't misled.",
